{"content":[{"c":["BRIMSTONE*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Old name for the nonmetallic element sulfur, literally “the stone that burns.” Sulfur ignites at a relatively low temperature and burns to produce acrid fumes of sulfur dioxide. Sulfur occurs naturally in volcanic regions such as the valley of the Dead Sea. “Fire and brimstone” are strongly associated in the Bible with divine retribution (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.19.24","r":"Gen.19.24","rawR":"Gen.19.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.19.24","value":"Gen.19.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 19:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.29.23","r":"Deut.29.23","rawR":"Deut.29.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.29.23","value":"Deut.29.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 29:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.18.15","r":"Job.18.15","rawR":"Job.18.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.18.15","value":"Job.18.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 18:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.11.6","r":"Ps.11.6","rawR":"Ps.11.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.11.6","value":"Ps.11.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 11:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.38.22","r":"Ezek.38.22","rawR":"Ezek.38.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.38.22","value":"Ezek.38.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 38:22"},"; and in ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.17.29","r":"Luke.17.29","rawR":"Luke.17.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.17.29","value":"Luke.17.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 17:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.9.17-18","r":"Rev.9.17-18","rawR":"Rev.9.17-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.9.17-18","value":"Rev.9.17-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rv 9:17-18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.14.10","r":"Rev.14.10","rawR":"Rev.14.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.14.10","value":"Rev.14.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.19.20","r":"Rev.19.20","rawR":"Rev.19.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.19.20","value":"Rev.19.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.20.10","r":"Rev.20.10","rawR":"Rev.20.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.20.10","value":"Rev.20.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.21.8","r":"Rev.21.8","rawR":"Rev.21.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.21.8","value":"Rev.21.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:8"},"). The last volcanic eruptions in Israel, which radiocarbon dating indicates took place about 4,000 years ago, probably left an impression on the inhabitants of the area that was passed on for generations. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MineralsandMetals_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MineralsandMetals_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MineralsandMetals_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Minerals and Metals"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Brimstone","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 19:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.19.24","rawQueryValue":"Gen.19.24","sourceRefExact":"Gen.19.24"},{"anchorText":"Dt 29:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.29.23","rawQueryValue":"Deut.29.23","sourceRefExact":"Deut.29.23"},{"anchorText":"Jb 18:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.18.15","rawQueryValue":"Job.18.15","sourceRefExact":"Job.18.15"},{"anchorText":"Ps 11:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.11.6","rawQueryValue":"Ps.11.6","sourceRefExact":"Ps.11.6"},{"anchorText":"Ez 38:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.38.22","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.38.22","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.38.22"},{"anchorText":"Lk 17:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.17.29","rawQueryValue":"Luke.17.29","sourceRefExact":"Luke.17.29"},{"anchorText":"Rv 9:17-18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rev.9.17-18","rawQueryValue":"Rev.9.17-18